 credits and other accounts receivable, that establish a claim for repayment. For some countries these claims include credit to public enterprises. This indicator is expressed as a percentage of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) which is the total income earned through the production of goods and services in an economic territory during an accounting period.','',2,7),(3339,'fdis_any_dfcl_cogn_all','Persons in food insecure households (% persons with  any degree of cognitive difficulty)','','',92,3),(3340,'fh1.11','Sent domestic remittances, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3341,'fh1.12','Sent domestic remittances, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3342,'fh1.fh2.11','Sent or received domestic remittances, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3343,'fh1.fh2.12','Sent or received domestic remittances, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3344,'fh2.11','Received domestic remittances, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3345,'fh2.12','Received domestic remittances, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3346,'fh2a.11','Received international remittances , out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3347,'fh2a.12','Received international remittances , in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3348,'FI.RES.GOLD.CD','Gold Holdings at London market price (US$ end period)','','',57,3),(3349,'FI.RES.GOLD.CD.WB','Gold, valued at year-end London prices (current US$)','The gold component of reserves is valued at year-end (December 31) London prices.  ','',11,3),(3350,'FI.RES.TOTL.CD.WB','Total reserves including gold valued at London gold price (current US$)','Gross international reserves comprise holdings of monetary gold, special drawing rights, the reserve position of members in the International Monetary Fund (IMF), and holdings of foreign exchange under the control of monetary authorities. The gold component is valued at end-of-year London prices. ','',11,3),(3351,'FI.RES.TOTL.CD.ZS','Total reserves includes gold (% of GDP)','Total reserves comprise holdings of monetary gold, special drawing rights, reserves of IMF members held by the IMF, and holdings of foreign exchange under the control of monetary authorities. The gold component of these reserves is valued at year-end (December 31) London prices. ','',11,3),(3352,'FI.RES.TOTL.DT.ZS','Total reserves (% of total external debt)','Reserve assets are external assets, including monetary gold, that are readily available to and controlled by monetary authorities for meeting balance of payments financing needs, for intervention in exchange markets to affect the currency exchange rate, and for other related purposes (such as maintaining confidence in the currency and the economy, and serving as a basis for foreign borrowing). Reserve assets must be denominated and settled in foreign currency. This indicator is expressed as a percentage of total external debt which are all liabilities that require payment(s) of interest and/or principal by the debtor at some point(s) in the future and that are owed to non-residents by residents of an economy.','',2,7),(3353,'FI.RES.TOTL.MO','Total reserves in months of imports','Reserve assets are external assets, including monetary gold, that are readily available to and controlled by monetary authorities for meeting balance of payments financing needs, for intervention in exchange markets to affect the currency exchange rate, and for other related purposes (such as maintaining confidence in the currency and the economy, and serving as a basis for foreign borrowing). Reserve assets must be denominated and settled in foreign currency. This item is expressed in terms of the number of months of imports of goods and services they could pay for [X/(Imports/12)].','',2,7),(3354,'FI.RES.TOTL.MO.WB','Total reserves in months of imports of goods and services','The number of months for which a country\'s reserves can sustain its imports. Gross international reserves comprise holdings of monetary gold, special drawing rights, the reserve position of members in the International Monetary Fund (IMF), and holdings of foreign exchange under the control of monetary authorities. The gold component is valued at end-of-year London prices. Imports of goods, services and income is the sum of goods (merchandise) imports, imports of (nonfactor) services and income (factor) payments.  Data are in current US dollars. ','',11,3),(3355,'fiaccount.t.d.11','Bank or similar financial institution account, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3356,'fiaccount.t.d.12','Bank or similar financial institution account, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3357,'fin10.11','Owns a credit card, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3358,'fin10.12','Owns a credit card, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3359,'fin11_1.11','Ever had an account at a bank or similar bank or similar financial institution, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3360,'fin11_1.12','Ever had an account at a bank or similar bank or similar financial institution, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3361,'fin11_2a.11','Can use account at a bank or similar financial institution without help if opened, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3362,'fin11_2a.12','Can use account at a bank or similar financial institution without help if opened, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3363,'fin11a.11','No account because bank or similar financial institutions are too far away, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3364,'fin11a.12','No account because bank or similar financial institutions are too far away, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3365,'fin11b.11','No account because financial services are too expensive, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3366,'fin11b.12','No account because financial services are too expensive, in laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3367,'fin11c.11','No account because of a lack of necessary documentation, out of laborforce (% age 15+)','','',28,3),(3368,'fin11c.12','No account becaus